# item27n: Banque01 story route, walked. Replaces the item27l route's remaining teleports where
# the decoded engine behavior measurably supports the walk; any kept teleport carries a measured
# cause. Objective 0 "Access the strongroom." completes through the game's own chain (Cine15
# Jones scene -> `event fin_flash` -> XIIIDispatcher4 -> GT_quitterbanque -> XIIIGoalTrigger0) and
# objective 1 "Escape from the bank." through Cine11's `playerevent fin_map` -> XIIIGoalTrigger2
# -> DoTravel -> Amos01, exactly as in item24/item27k/item27l.
#
# item86 re-time on the integrated engine-fidelity tree (volume-brush overlap, item81c):
# `AActor::IsOverlapping` now dispatches a volume brush to its `Brush` UModel BSP (see
# crates/xiii-script/src/brush.rs), so a DetectionVolume fires on its real brush shape instead of
# the class cylinder anchored on its Location. DetectionVolume12 (Event `jones_dial`, starting
# Cine15) is a 6-plane box in world space: x in (-7824,-7616), y in (-2784,-2336), z in (784,1248)
# (measured, `xiii-tool props` + the decoded primitive). Its Location (-7616,-2784,1456) is the
# platform-top corner, ABOVE the brush (z 1456 > 1248): the old teleport-to-Location touch at
# t=93.017 no longer fires, and the volume now fires while the player walks into the brush on the
# safe level (z 875). The route therefore enters the brush first, then visits Jones, then the
# walkway, so Cine15's own `wait player 300` gates (actions [3] and [34]) pass in order.
#
# item27m teleport-1 fix (the t=13 key spot): Engine.dll execCanSee (0x1036f070) -> SeePawn
# (0x1036dc40) -> LineOfSightTo (0x1036ac70) decoded; the VM now traces the engine's lines (base
# Location first, then the Enemy eye point without distance limits or the 0.8*CollisionHeight top
# with 8000^2/2000^2 limits) and applies SeePawn's SightRadius/Visibility range gate. Unit tests
# in crates/xiii-script/src/vm_tests.rs (line_of_sight_to_*, can_see_*); the customer-side release
# measured in local/re/item27m/probe-customer.log. The t=13 teleport is GONE.
#
# Walked story chain (all measured in probe-u/probe-t runs, cine trace):
#   - spawn -> DetectionVolume1 (touch starts Cine1, the teller scene).
#   - walk to the counter spot (-330,-2133): Cine1[12] "wait player 300" (vs the teller at
#     (-494,-2133)) passes; the customer queue maze is walkable (probe-m).
#   - Cine1[16] "wait event recoit_cle" then needs Banque0.STA_DonneCle.Tick to see
#     VSize2D(teller-player)<300 && CanSee(teller). The item27m engine sight fix releases the
#     key from the walked customer side; no lobby teleport remains.
#   - walk the staff corridor north to (-540,-1350): the teller's Cine1[32] "wait player 500"
#     (vs her at (-567,-1284) after `opendoor porte7`) passes.
#   - walk west to (-1560,-1290) and WAIT: the double armored door XIIIMover14/15
#     ("bankporteblindee1") opens only for the teller's Cine1[39] `playerevent porteblindee1`
#     (t~37.4); pushing it earlier wedges (probe-t v2).
#   - follow the teller's own measured waypoints down the stair corridor ((-1717,-1440) ->
#     (-1772,-1940) -> (-1818,-2250), z 107 -> -149): Cine1[43] "wait player 1500", Cine6[4]
#     "wait player 700" (James at (-1859,-2574)) and Cine1[51] "wait player 400" (vs the teller
#     at (-1974,-2418)) all pass on foot. Her chain then fires `event coffre`/`event choatoi`
#     (the vault key), `event toto` (t~50.6, unlocks the vault door Porte8) and Cine6[17]
#     `event coffreserrure` (t~53.7) which OPENS Porte12 (the "coffreentree" door).
#   - walk the whole vault corridor on foot: through Porte12, down the ramp to z=-149, around
#     the bankescaroulant block (east side), south along x~=-2300, west along y~=-6100, to the
#     vault door (-2840,-6397). Touches fire the game's own actors: Porte12, Trigger15,
#     BreakableMover0, Porte8, TriggerSound6/11/14, XIIIMover6/27, and XIIIDispatcher5 (the
#     briefcase `debut_flash` chain); Porte20/21 (the vault door panels) open by themselves.
#     The t=44 vault teleport of the old route is gone entirely.
#   - Teleport to DetectionVolume12's platform (-7616,-2784,1456) — re-measured on this tree
#     (item73/item75; item93 with input walks): there is still NO walkable connection between
#     the vault level (z=-149) and the strongroom (z 800-1504). The safe-level wall is Model69
#     x=-6976 (z 800..1312, y -2752..512), the platform-level east wall x=-7360 (z 1312..1504),
#     and the platform corridor is ringed by Model69 walls y=-2752/-2368 (z 1296..1504) and
#     x=-8512; the nav graph has no point west of x=-6900. The vault's LadderVolume5 climbs a
#     capped Model69 shaft (volume top z=256, walls to 800, no floor above -224) and delivers
#     nothing (item93 E-LAD2). The authored return walk from the vault door (item93 E-T1c)
#     reaches only the ground-floor corridor; every strongroom approach is one of the sealed
#     faces above. The teleport lands the player on the platform and the walk delivers
#     DetectionVolume12's own engine Touch at t=96.6 (measured, this run).
#   - item86 strongroom walk: from the platform the player walks SW into DV12's brush
#     (t=96 goto -7693 -2564; brush contains (-7693.4,-2564.8,875), measured), which fires
#     DV12 -> Cine15 at t=96.583. It then returns along the walkway line to Jones's spot
#     (-7161,-2141) for Cine15[3] "wait player 300" (t=103 goto), and continues west to the
#     walkway (-7883,-2648) for Cine15[34] "wait player 300" (t=109 goto). The direct return
#     from the brush to Jones stalls at (-7522,-2370) (measured; a wall/gap between the brush
#     mouth and Jones's ledge), so the route passes the walkway waypoint (-7522,-2490) first:
#     the player reaches Jones at t=104.5 and the walkway at t=111 (measured). Cine15's own
#     dialogue/anims then run to `event fin_flash` at t=127.1 (measured), and XIIIDispatcher4's
#     delay promotes objective 0 at t=140.1.
#   - Escape teleports TT5/TT2/TT3 stay — re-measured on this tree (item75; item93 with input
#     runs; item96 re-measures TT5's lift). The player is inside the sealed strongroom, so no
#     input walk can reach any escape volume; the teleports deliver each volume's own engine
#     Touch (the game's own code):
#     * TT5 (1300.03,-1917.39,1478): the lift cannot BOARD anyone — the ride itself works
#       (item96 E-A: a player standing on the cage floor is carried 1082 -> 1561.7 in lockstep
#       with the cage 1027 -> 1506.7; the item93 "no floor collision" cause was a sweep
#       artifact: the mesh's per-triangle collision set has the cabin floor at 991/1007), but
#       no input opens the cage: at rest all six lift doors sit at their zero-motion key 0
#       (Location constant while alpha animates; the decoded KeyPos[1] holds the open slides),
#       the ray use answers on the closed outer door LiftDoor3 (measured x2, E-B), and the only
#       button (LiftButton0, cage-internal) stays occluded behind the closed door plane. The
#       manager chain from a named button use rides the cage EMPTY (E-B). Walking on floor 2
#       within ~234 UU of TT5's axis does fire TouchTrigger5 without the fall (E-C, touch
#       t=2.133 at (1078,-1920)), but that zone is beyond the sealed pocket and fires ONLY
#       TouchTrigger5 ('vignracaille') — DetectionVolume18 ('Dispatch_cinefbi', brush over the
#       shaft mouth behind the closed ride-top doors LiftDoor4/5, blocking at the door face
#       x=1112) does not, so the walk would change the authored escape chain. The teleport
#       delivers both Touches and lands on LiftCage0's roof (centre 1317.1).
#     * TT2 (865,-4075,1530): the Model69 shaft wall y=-2080 (x 1136..1472, z 1488..1968) stops
#       the shaft side; the floor-2 corridor dead-ends on StaticMeshActor39 (desk top 1572)
#       against the Staticbanque.hall wall y=-3664 (z 1488..1952) under the z=1952 ceiling —
#       no jump-over even from the desk top (item93 probes).
#     * TT3 (1134,-4222,480): the banksortiescasecour tower encloses the TT2 landing: every
#       walk-off/jump from the tower top stalls on its 34.4 deg ramp face with the east cheek
#       x=998.2 (measured rests at x=964.2, y -4139/-4219/-4244/-4246), the ladder tower
#       (banksortiescasecour2 walls x=882/x=1045/y=-4378) and the trash bins close the rest,
#       and the courtyard walls (y=-3728 north with bins, y=-4864 south, the egout east, no
#       floor west of x=784) allow no street-side entry (item93 E-F/E-G). The teleport
#       placement delivers TouchTrigger3's and TouchTrigger11's Touches (both Event
#       'fbi_dial2', measured same-tick in the item93 mini-run) and Cine11 places the player
#       where TT4 fires on the natural fall to the courtyard floor (touch t=134.333); the yard
#       walk never reaches TT3's own cylinder (the walk line from the Cine11 position to TT3
#       is clear, but the delivery must come from above).
#   - item86 re-time of the escape flow: the four teleports move AFTER `fin_flash` (t=127.1):
#     TT5 t=128, TT2 t=131, TT3 t=134 (the old t=127/130/133 assumed DV12's t=93.017 touch, now
#     3.6 s later). They may overlap XIIIDispatcher4's 13 s delay (objective 0 at t=140.1). The
#     ending chain then completes as before (objective 1 at t=147, travel at t=183.0).
#   - TT10 (CarOut, 1014.38,-4309,609.458) has NO working delivery in this engine run and its
#     teleport was REMOVED (item73): the cutscene owns the player pose from t=133.017, and the
#     old t=139 teleport never relocated the player. The CarOut beat is absent here, not
#     delivered. Engine notes: TriggerEvent is TAG-matched; XIIIMover26 (Tag 'explocoffre_bis')
#     has no sender, and Trigger27 ('bombe') has Event=None so its Touch fires nothing. Each kept
#     teleport delivers the volume's own engine Touch, the game's own code.

